+<h2>127. The m365 success-redirect pin also refuses a connection id joined to the redirect by string concatenation (KS-1800)</h2>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>What this changes.</strong></td><td> One new scan in <code>Blockchain/Dev/services/m365-integration/src/__tests__/ks1670-the-success-redirect-encodes-the-connection-id.test.ts</code> (test only, +26 lines). It reads <code>m365-integration/src/index.ts</code> as text, drops comment lines, and refuses a <code>connectionId=</code> query key that is closed by a quote and joined to something with <code>+</code>. The existing cell R1 looks for the template text <code>connectionId=${</code>, so a redirect that carries the id by concatenation is invisible to it by construction; this is the other half, the gate-7 mutant N6 of KS 1670.
+    </td></tr><tr><td>Three new cells: R3 is RED when such a line exists; C4 is a control that the scan can fail (it finds a planted concatenated redirect, in either quote style); C5 is a control that the scan ignores a comment line and that the real template redirect is still in the source. The file now holds 8 cells. <strong>Zero product bytes</strong>: <code>index.ts</code> is unchanged (the tamper target is never committed).
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3>127.1 What proves it</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>Red under a tamper, green on the untouched product, and no other cell moves.</strong></td><td> <strong>Tamper, worktree only, never committed:</strong> appending <code>const rawRedirect = '/admin/integrations?m365=success&amp;connectionId=' + connectionId; void rawRedirect;</code> to line 677 of <code>index.ts</code> makes R3 fail: <strong>1 of 8 fail</strong>, the controls pass. The file was restored by content and the whole-file sha256 equals the pre-tamper value. <strong>Untouched product:</strong> 8 of 8 pass.
+    </td></tr><tr><td><strong>Whole m365-integration unit suite</strong> (vitest): develop <code>a8c554659cb3</code> 29 files / 277 cells, 277 pass; with the change 29 files / <strong>280 cells, 280 pass</strong>, 0 failed, 0 skipped. <code>tsc</code> with the test file in the program (39 source files, 29 under <code>__tests__</code>): <strong>0 errors</strong>, and a planted type error was reported once as <code>TS2322</code> by file name. <code>eslint</code> on the test file: 0 errors, 0 warnings, and a planted file raised <code>@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars</code> and <code>no-debugger</code>.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3>127.2 Environment and figures</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="1"><strong>Measured 2026-10-30 (UTC) on an Apple Silicon (arm64) Mac, macOS 27.0.1, shared with other seats.</strong></td><td> Develop <code>a8c554659cb3</code> with the change on top. Node v26.8.1 (not an LTS line), TypeScript 5.9.3, vitest 4.1.12, eslint 10.7.0.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3>127.3 What this does not prove</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>A text scan of one file, not a running service.</strong></td><td> KS-1800 stays open. Not done: N3 (an equivalent rewrite of the redirect turns R2 red), N4, and the wire cells A1, A3 and A7 the gate suggested. The scan reads <code>index.ts</code> non-comment lines only: a concatenation that does not spell <code>connectionId=</code> followed by a quote and <code>+</code> (for example a key built from parts) is invisible to it.
+    </td></tr><tr><td>Not run: the four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, Performance/k6), a running stack, Node 24, any deploy.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3>127.4 Running it</h3>
+<pre><code>cd Blockchain/Dev/services/m365-integration &amp;&amp; npm test -- src/__tests__/ks1670-the-success-redirect-encodes-the-connection-id.test.ts   # 8 cells in this file
+cd Blockchain/Dev/services/m365-integration &amp;&amp; npm test                                             # 29 files / 280 cells</code></pre>
